Description:
  Administration platform settings section body.

  Presents the administrator-overridable runtime settings: platform identity, the SEED System
  Company, outgoing mail, an explanation of the configuration model, and the expired-record
  maintenance controls. Every setting here resolves through RuntimeSettings as a database row,
  then the deployment default, then a built-in default, so an absent override is a normal state
  rather than an error.

  Infrastructure values are deliberately absent. Database credentials, the application key, the
  application URL and domain, and the cookie and session settings are never exposed here.

  The SEED System Company card is guarded twice: once on the permission that may manage seed
  infrastructure, and once on whether the shared company row actually exists, because a database
  older than the v0.5.8 baseline has no row to edit and must say so rather than fail on save.

  WARNING: a template comment is not a safe place to document syntax. F3 parses its own tags
  inside comments, so a tag written out as a usage example becomes a real tag in the compiled
  template. A comment delimiter written inside a comment body ends it early and leaks the
  remainder onto the page. Keep every comment plain prose: no angle brackets, no comment
  delimiters, no template tokens and no code, not even to document one.
